        "link": "https://www.scmp.com/news/china/diplomacy/article/3350054/china-hits-out-dangerous-and-irresponsible-us-blockade-irans-ports?utm_source=rss_feed",
        "orario": "13:00",
        "timestamp": 1776164408,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement US-China relations China Diplomacy China hits out at ‘dangerous and irresponsible’ US blockade of Iran’s ports Beijing says American move will ‘inflame tensions, escalate the situation and undermine an already fragile ceasefire’ 2 -MIN READ 2 -MIN Phoebe Zhang in Shenzhen Published: 7:00pm, 14 Apr 2026 China has slammed the US blockade of Iranian ports as “dangerous and irresponsible”, calling for an immediate and full ceasefire and for the Strait of Hormuz to be reopened. Foreign ministry spokesman Guo Jiakun told reporters at a daily briefing in Beijing on Tuesday that the US action would only “inflame tensions, escalate the situation and undermine an already fragile ceasefire”, and that would further jeopardise the safety of navigation in the strait. “We urge all parties to abide by the ceasefire arrangement, focus on the broader direction of dialogue and negotiations, take concrete actions to de-escalate the regional situation and restore normal navigation in the strait at an early date,” Guo said. Advertisement He added that the situation in the region was “at a critical stage” and said China would continue to work with the international community to promote peace talks and to strive for peace and stability in the Middle East. The US began a naval blockade of Iranian ports on Monday after its marathon peace talks with Iran in Pakistan to reopen the Strait of Hormuz failed over the weekend . Iranians dismiss Trump threats to block Hormuz Strait Iranians dismiss Trump threats to block Hormuz Strait The US Central Command on Monday issued a formal notice to seafarers outlining enforcement measures in waters around the strait, saying that not all maritime traffic would be halted. The blockade “will not impede neutral transit passage through the Strait of Hormuz to or from non-Iranian destinations”, it said. Advertisement Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
